---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SUBSTACK_URL } from '../consts';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What The Voyager collects (very little) and why.">
	<article class="prose">
		<p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p><em>Last updated: 13 October 2026.</em></p>

		<p>
			The short version: the site collects very little. It does not sell your data. It may show ads from Google
			AdSense, and if it does, Google and its partners use cookies for that, as explained below.
		</p>

		<h2>Hosting</h2>
		<p>
			The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes basic request data
			(such as IP address and browser type) to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse. See
			<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Advertising</h2>
		<p>
			The Voyager may show ads served by Google AdSense. Google, as a third-party vendor, uses cookies to serve
			ads based on your visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies lets it and its
			partners show ads to you based on your visit to this site and other sites on the internet.
		</p>
		<p>
			You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
			<a href="https://adssettings.google.com">Google Ads Settings</a>, or opt out of some third-party vendors'
			use of cookies for personalised advertising at
			<a href="https://www.aboutads.info">aboutads.info</a>. See also
			<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">how Google uses data from sites that use its
			services</a>.
		</p>
		<p>
			Where the law requires it (for example in the EU, the UK and Switzerland), you are asked for your consent
			before advertising cookies are used, and you can change your choice later. Ads are never placed in the
			newsletter.
		</p>

		<h2>Analytics</h2>
		<p>
			<!-- TODO: update this if you turn on Cloudflare Web Analytics. -->
			No analytics are running yet. If that changes, it will be privacy-friendly, cookie-free page counts
			(Cloudflare Web Analytics), and this page will say so.
		</p>

		<h2>Newsletter</h2>
		<p>
			The sign-up form is an embedded form from Substack. If you subscribe, Substack stores your email
			address and handles sending the newsletter, under
			<a href="https://substack.com/privacy">Substack's privacy policy</a>. You can unsubscribe from any
			email. The newsletter lives at <a href={SUBSTACK_URL}>{SUBSTACK_URL.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Your browser</h2>
		<p>
			If you pick light or dark mode with the theme button, that choice is saved in your browser's local
			storage. It never leaves your device.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about privacy? Use the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
		</p>
	</article>
</Base>
